---
source: misc/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"getopt\")"
---
Parse command options (enhanced)

Usage: getopt optstring parameters
       getopt [options] [--] optstring parameters
       getopt [options] -o|--options optstring [--] parameters

Arguments:
  [PARAMS]...  Parameters to parse

Options:
  -a, --alternative                Allow long options to start with a single -
  -l, --longoptions <LONGOPTIONS>  Long options to recognize (comma-separated)
  -n, --name <NAME>                Program name for error messages
  -o, --options <OPTIONS>          Short options string to recognize
  -q, --quiet                      Disable error output from getopt
  -Q, --quiet-output               Suppress normal output
  -s, --shell <SHELL>              Set quoting conventions for shell (sh, bash, csh, tcsh) [default:
                                   bash]
  -T, --test                       Test for enhanced getopt version (returns exit code 4)
  -u, --unquoted                   Don't quote the output
  -h, --help                       Print help
